  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Symmetry in \\(x,\\) \\(y\\) makes the operation commutative. Also, \\[ \\frac1{x*y}=\\frac1x+\\frac1y. \\] Thus both \\((x*y)*z\\) and \\(x*(y*z)\\) have reciprocal \\(\\frac1x+\\frac1y+\\frac1z,\\) so they are equal. The operation is associative too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "The formula is visibly unchanged when \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are interchanged",
        "Rewrite the operation through its reciprocal: \\(\\frac1{x*y}=\\frac1x+\\frac1y\\)"
      ],
